<h2>Text</h2>

<p>
  Text is made of a few tags: <c><h1></c> to <c><h3></c> for headings, <c><p></c> for paragraphs, with <b>bold</b>, <i>italic</i>,
  <c>inline code</c> and <a href="https://example.com">links</a> inside.
</p>

<ol>
  <li>numbered lists with <c><ol></c></li>
  <li>bullets with <c><ul></c>, nested lists inside an <c><li></c></li>
</ol>

<quote>A <c><quote></c> gets an accent bar.</quote>

<p>
  A slide without code is centered on the screen, like this one: the deck says so with <c>textOnly</c> in <c>deck.json</c>.
</p>

<notes>
  The notes tag holds the speaker notes. They never show on the slide. Open the presenter window with p.
</notes>
